ence is we knew the prime  minister was breaking the rules  we didn't know we do i mean the police  but we knew he was in breach yeah but  kia stammer was judging what the police  might decide well right  he was a former director of public  prostitution you can't do that yes  that's right but but but but we know  that the difference is immense holding  regular parties at number 10 downing  street during the lockdown that the  prime minister pretended he hadn't been  at and then it turns out he was he stood  in prime minister's questions and said  he was angry at what allegra stratton  his press secretary has said about a  party which he said hadn't happened and  we later find out he'd been at it he was  lying through his teeth to the british  public and it is that disreputable  behavior that brings all of politics and  all politicians into disrepute kirstama  is sending a clear message that he is  not like that he has integrity if he is  issued with a fine for breaching the  rules he will resign the prime minister  should adopt exactly that same position  if he wants to uphold the integrity of  standards in public life how do you feel  about the northern ireland protocol  being ripped up  well this is this is a really dangerous  move for the for the government to want  to make at this stage and we need to  remember  how the northern ireland protocol came  into being in the first place boris  johnson negotiated it it was part of the  brexit deal that back in 2019 the prime  minister uh came and said was an  oven-ready brexit deal it was a good  deal for britain um everything in it was  sorted and resolved and we must vote for  it and indeed the public did go out and  vote for that brexit deal further down  the line it turns out as as as as often  as this prime minister he'd lied he said  there would be no border down the irish  sea over his dead body there only would  be a border down the rsc over his dead  body in fact there is a border down the  irish sea because u